{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774300461,"nonce":"BlHAVuCKG5PzBQ9y8lysroP0yWA=","message":"## Implementation Spec\n\n### 1. New fields on EvaluationRecord (database.py ~line 162)\n\nAdd four new Optional[dict[str, Any]] fields with JSON column type:\n\n- **perturbation_config**: Perturbation type and parameters (amplitudes, where applied, etc.)\n- **task_variants**: Task variant definitions used in evaluation (variant keys → parameter overrides)\n- **sisu_params**: SISU values evaluated (if applicable)\n- **eval_setup_params**: Catch-all for any additional setup_eval_tasks_and_models parameters\n\nAll default to None for backward compatibility with existing records. SQLAlchemy JSON type is already mapped for dict[str, Any] via RecordBase.type_annotation_map.\n\n### 2. Update generate_eval_hash() (~line 1020)\n\nAdd an optional `eval_setup_metadata: Optional[dict[str, Any]]` parameter. When provided, serialize it to a canonical JSON string (sorted keys) and include it in the hash input. This ensures different evaluation setups produce different hashes.\n\n### 3. Update add_evaluation() (~line 1046)\n\nAdd optional keyword parameters matching the new EvaluationRecord fields. Pass them through to:\n- generate_eval_hash() as eval_setup_metadata (merged into a single dict for hashing)\n- EvaluationRecord constructor\n- Also update existing records when hash matches (update the metadata fields)\n\n### 4. Update setup_eval_for_module() (execution.py ~line 254)\n\nAfter constructing task_variants and before calling add_evaluation(), extract the relevant metadata from hps and the analysis_module, and pass it through:\n- perturbation_config from hps.train.pert (type, std, etc.)\n- task_variants from the constructed task_variants dict\n- eval_setup_params as a catch-all\n\n### 5. Add query helper: query_evaluations_by_setup()\n\nA new function in database.py that filters EvaluationRecord by JSON field contents (e.g., find all evaluations with a specific perturbation type). Uses SQLAlchemy JSON path queries or Python-side filtering.","files":null}]}